defklown wrote:
> Is there any way to ID the luckstone in "The Catacombs" version of
> Mine's End? That's the version in which you begin in a 5x9 room with
> two hidden doors; one on each side. The rest of the floor is mazelike.
> Every possible luckstone position is in a corner, and you can't pickaxe
> through the walls around the possible luckstone positions. Do I lure a
> gnome or something towards a suspected luckstone and see if he picks it
> up? What do you do in this situation?

There are three possible random places where the luck stone and a flint
stone may be located, and on those two places where the stones are there
are also level teleporters. But there are also random gems/stone created
on that level, so you cannot be absolutely sure that there's not also a
loadstone. I generally pick up both stone take them to the minetown and
ask for their price; the one with a price of around 60 zorkmids is the
luckstone and the one with a price of just 5 (or so) zorkmids is flint.
Use the minetown altar to identify its BUC status.

